<!-- Golden case H: a Ziffer billed once per patient is not a duplicate.

     Three invoices, three different `<abrechnungsfall>` — three different patients — and each one
     is billed GOÄ 1 (Beratung) exactly once. Nothing is repeated anywhere: every billing case
     holds one line, and the three cases are audited in three separate Soufflé runs.

     `audit_delivery` used to run its duplicate-Ziffer check over `delivery.positions()`, which is
     every invoice in the delivery flattened into one list. On this delivery that produced two
     warnings reading "GOÄ 1 kommt mehrfach vor (Positionen 1 und 1)" — and on a real twenty-invoice
     ADL delivery, nineteen of them. Every one was false. The sentence the finding makes ("die
     Regelprüfung betrachtet eine Ziffer nur einmal") is true only inside a single fact base, which
     has been a single `<abrechnungsfall>` since the cross-patient fix (case F), so a Ziffer
     appearing on two patients' invoices is not folded away and there is nothing to warn about. A
     billing centre reading a Prüfbericht for their second delivery would have had to sort nineteen
     spurious warnings from the real findings, with no invoice id on any of them to sort by.

     Expected: **zero** `padnext_duplicate_ziffer` findings, three `chargeable` positions,
     `confirmed_wrong_eur` 0.00, and 32.16 € in `unconfirmed` — the same honest reading case A and
     case F get, because no verified rule bears on a lone GOÄ 1 either.

     `tests/golden/case_c_verified_factor_cap/` is the case that shows the check still fires where
     it should not be silenced: it bills GOÄ 440 twice, and the two lines sit on two separate
     billing cases, so its duplicate warning was spurious for the same reason and is gone too. A
     genuine repeat — one Ziffer twice on ONE `<abrechnungsfall>` — is still reported, now naming
     the invoice it is in.

     Synthetic data throughout: echtdaten="0". -->
